# CVEs Trivy may skip in the image scan (build-image-stage.yml, build-image-prod.yml).
# Only for a vulnerability with no fixed package available yet. One ID per line,
# with a comment: package, fixed version, and when to remove the line.
# The image refreshes apk packages daily (APK_REFRESH), so a fixed package is
# picked up on the next day's build.
# CVE-2026-86144: libxml2 2.13.9-r2; the fix (2.13.9-r3) is only in Alpine edge and not yet in Alpine 3.24.
# Track: https://pkgs.alpinelinux.org/packages?name=libxml2&branch=v3.24
# Remove once Alpine 3.24 ships libxml2 >= 2.13.9-r3.
CVE-2026-86144
# CVE-2026-107891: musl, musl-utils 1.2.6-r3; Trivy expects 1.2.6-r6, the version that fixes it in Alpine edge.
# Alpine 3.24 lists the CVE as fixed in 1.2.6-r3 (https://secdb.alpinelinux.org/v3.24/main.json), which the image has.
# Track: https://pkgs.alpinelinux.org/packages?name=musl&branch=v3.24
# Remove once Alpine 3.24 ships musl >= 1.2.6-r6, or Trivy stops reporting it for 1.2.6-r3.
CVE-2026-107891
